
naive_bayes_classifier.py   Main Python classifier script
fake_or_real_news.csv       Dataset (6,335 labeled news articles)
pipeline_results.csv        Output: metrics table (auto-generated)
figures/                    Output: all 6 figures (auto-generated)
README.txt                  

libraries:
  pandas
  numpy
  matplotlib
  seaborn
  scikit-learn
  nltk


Install all dependencies with one command: 
pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn scikit-learn nltk

If given an error
>>> import nltk
>>> nltk.download('stopwords')
run command: python -m nltk.downloader stopwords
Then run the python file

Data Set:

Source: Lutz Hamel (2021). "Fake or Real News Dataset."
        https://github.com/lutzhamel/fake-news
6,335 labeled news articles (3,164 fake, 3,171 real).


Output: 

fig1_f1_comparison.png      F1 score horizontal bar chart by pipeline
fig2_confusion_matrix.png   Confusion matrix for best model
fig3_roc_curves.png         ROC curves with AUC for all pipelines
fig4_top_features.png       Top 20 predictive words per class
fig5_metrics_comparison.png Grouped bar chart of all 4 metrics
fig6_cv_f1.png              5-fold CV F1 with error bars
